<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  SignPath artifact configuration for WARDEN.

  The GitHub workflow uploads the two installers with actions/upload-artifact,
  which always delivers them as one ZIP, so the root element is <zip-file> and
  each installer is matched inside it. Paste this into SignPath
  (Project → Artifact Configurations) and use the resulting slug in the
  SIGNPATH_ARTIFACT_CONFIGURATION_SLUG repository variable.

  The namespace is the schema SignPath validates against, and it is versioned:
  `http://signpath.io/artifact-configuration/v1`, not the bare
  `http://signpath.io/artifact-configuration`. An artifact configuration that
  fails validation is rejected when it is created, so the bare form never
  reaches a signing request — but a copy kept in the repository is what someone
  pastes months later, and it has to be the file that works.

  product-name is a constraint, not a label: SignPath signs the installer only
  if its embedded version resource says WARDEN, which is what electron-builder
  writes from `productName` in electron-builder.yml. The SignPath Foundation
  terms require signed binaries to carry enforced metadata attributes, and this
  is the one that cannot be faked by building something else and calling it
  WARDEN. If the product name ever changes, this file has to change with it or
  the signing request is refused.

  Only the two shipped installers are signed. The payload executable inside the
  NSIS installer keeps whatever signature it was built with; signing it as well
  requires signing win-unpacked\WARDEN.exe before packaging, which SignPath
  cannot do from a single archived artifact.
-->
<artifact-configuration xmlns="http://signpath.io/artifact-configuration/v1">
  <zip-file>
    <pe-file path="WARDEN-Setup-*.exe" product-name="WARDEN">
      <authenticode-sign hash-algorithm="sha256" description="WARDEN installer" />
    </pe-file>
    <pe-file path="WARDEN-Portable-*.exe" product-name="WARDEN">
      <authenticode-sign hash-algorithm="sha256" description="WARDEN portable" />
    </pe-file>
  </zip-file>
</artifact-configuration>
